-- Named rejection: a LOCAL ASSUME, which the top-level widening deliberately
-- did not travel to.
--
-- A top-level ASSUME now lowers to an input predicate: it has a module-level
-- name, so a target can declare it, a scenario editor can state it and an
-- interview can abduce it. A local one has none of that — it is scoped to one
-- definition's WHERE block, there is nothing to declare it as, and nothing for
-- an interview to ask about. The two sites are a few hundred lines apart in
-- `L4.Relational.Lower` and the careless version of the widening takes both;
-- this fixture is what fails if it does.
--
-- The diagnostic is `local ASSUME`, distinct from every kind the top-level path
-- can produce, because #258 §6.1's rejection census counts by kind.

@export
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `above the threshold` IF n AT LEAST threshold
  WHERE
    ASSUME threshold IS A NUMBER
